WEBVTT

00:11:29.871 --> 00:11:32.079
And I think people definitely got

00:11:32.079 --> 00:11:35.037
and still are overexcited
about 3:00 today,

00:11:35.204 --> 00:11:37.204
but still probably underestimated

00:11:37.204 --> 00:11:39.746
the potential of where these models
will go in the future.

00:11:40.162 --> 00:11:43.787
And so maybe there's this like short term
overhyped and long term under hype

00:11:44.121 --> 00:11:48.246
for the entire field, for tax models, for
whatever you'd like. It's going on.

00:11:48.412 --> 00:11:51.496
And as you said, there's clearly
some gibberish in there.

00:11:51.704 --> 00:11:54.204
But on the other hand, those were
like well-formed sentences.

00:11:54.204 --> 00:11:56.371
And there were a couple of ideas
and there that I was like, oh,

00:11:56.412 --> 00:11:58.787
like they actually maybe that's right.

00:11:58.996 --> 00:12:04.287
And I think if artificial intelligence,
even in its current very larval state,